# Best Practices

When deploying Microsoft Sentinel:

- Connect only required data sources.
- Develop high-quality Analytics Rules.
- Continuously tune detections.
- Use Automation Rules to reduce manual work.
- Apply Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).
- Monitor data ingestion costs.
- Integrate Threat Intelligence.
- Review incidents regularly.
- Document investigation procedures.
- Conduct periodic detection validation.

---

# Common Challenges

Organizations implementing Microsoft Sentinel often encounter:

- Excessive alert volume
- False positives
- Poor-quality log sources
- High ingestion costs
- Inconsistent naming conventions
- Limited KQL expertise
- Incomplete data collection
- Manual investigation processes

Addressing these challenges requires ongoing tuning, governance, and analyst training.

